* ''Light, lend, wear'' (operator, 2026-11-17: //"True up the memes, focus on isomorphic by intent but set in place the node integration now. We'll handle the browser side after the merge."//; the design at lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/light-lend-wear; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/the-worn-house#/the-pulama`>>, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/the-lit-set`>>). Three acts carry what "open" blurred: the human ''lights'' faces at the pūlama (these faces' keys stand ready); the pūlama ''lends'' one vessel a named set of faces, one kūkulu lei per lent face, each strung by that face's own hand, and partial lighting serves the lit faces and names the ones waiting; a session ''wears'' one face inside the lent set, and the vessel wears none. The pūlama's bond takes the name ''the lend'' (//hospitium//); "session" names the one-face wearer alone. The node's single mounted face reads as ''the daemon mount'', with its honest limit: every lent face writes through that one daemon island until a daemon per face stands (`C13`, rank 34). The node lend set rides rank 2b, the browser's rank 4d.

